Source: https://github.com/advplyr/audiobookshelf
Official image: docker.io/advplyr/audiobookshelf

The upstream source and Docker image are unmodified. All integration is under
synology/. image-lock.json records the release source, immutable multi-platform
index, platform manifests and configuration digests. Container Manager normally
downloads the image; the SPK does not contain its layers. The integration's MIT
license does not relicense Audiobookshelf or its image dependencies. Retain their
notices and provide corresponding source when redistributing GPL-covered code.
The upstream Dockerfile and package lockfiles document its Node, FFmpeg, SQLite,
Alpine and JavaScript dependency build inputs. No complete image-license audit is
claimed. The upstream icon is reused unchanged under the upstream project license.
Scaffold notices are preserved in LICENSES/TEMPLATE.txt.

